(c) THE PRETOKENIZER IS A WALL: no token may span a regex split boundary.
  SPLIT_PATTERN = '(?i:[sdmt]|ll|ve|re)|[^\r\n\p{L}\p{N}]?+\p{L}+|\p{N}{1,2}| ?[^\s\p{L}\p{N}]++[\r\n]*|\s*[\r\n]|\s+(?!\S)|\s+
     'hello world' -> ['hell', 'o', ' world']
        ' the the' -> [' the', ' the']
         '1234567' -> ['12', '34', '56', '7']
       '  \n\n  x' -> ['  ', '\n\n', ' ', ' x']
  Note ' the the' never merges into one token and \p{N}{1,2} caps digit runs at 2,
  so 1234567 can never become a single token no matter how frequent it is.

